# Code ownership for runlog-vocabularies.
#
# Vocabulary data is consumed by both the runlog server (sanitizer) and the
# verifier (pre-sign check) — a malicious or careless edit here would
# weaken the default-deny gate for every Runlog submission. So every change
# to allow-list data, the scope registry, the validator, and CI configuration
# gets owner review before merge.
#
# A single catch-all rule is sufficient for a single-owner repo: per-path
# entries pointing to the same owner add no review-routing value and
# silently drift out of sync as the layout grows. Re-introduce per-path
# rules only when ownership genuinely diverges (e.g. a domain-expert
# co-owner for `protocols/` while `domains/` stays with the original
# maintainer).

